  "body": "Part of #4023. Step K4 of the record (K0, #4024; in `RECOMMENDED.md` under the heading `#4024`, migration order). It is delivered on `side/path-kernel` (AGENTS.md **Side branch**). It builds on K1 (#4025) and K2 (the guide stage).\n\n## What to do\n\nAdd the order stage and the link stage to `camcraft-pathkernel`, behind the traits `OrderPlanner` and `LinkProof`.\n\n- Order: the start side (Inside, Outside, Auto) and the cut direction change only the order of the curves and the start point of each curve (law 3). The output is a permutation of the input curves.\n- Link: the tool stays down between two cuts when an in-plane link is proved clear. A lift is permitted only when an in-plane link would cut the part or a fixture, and each lift has a named reason (the link rule; maintainer, #3741).\n- The link law of the present ring links (#3747) is the start. The air-plan chain and link law of the Adaptive strategy joins the split pieces of an Outside band (the decision of the record for #3934).\n- The link parts of #3757 (2D Contour) and #3758 (Trace, Engrave, 2D Chamfer) are covered by this stage.\n- No old planner changes. With the default switch the output is identical.\n\n## Pins\n\n- The stage is registered in the law suite (#4027) and passes L3 and the link rule.\n- On the disc and the dog bone with the material side Outside: 0 crossing feeds, and a named reason for each lift. The record's target is 0 lifts on the disc. Give the measured count with the measures of #4154.\n- Negative tests: a link that crosses an island is refused; a lift with no reason is refused.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe order stage and the link stage are on the side branch with their pins green. K3 (load control) can then start.\n",
